<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Faizabad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Faizabad is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Ghaghara river beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayodhya">Ayodhya</a>. It grew in the 1730s as the residence of the early nawabs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a>, Saadat Ali Khan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safdar-jang">Safdar Jang</a>, and was the capital of Awadh until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asaf-ud-daula">Asaf-ud-Daula</a> moved his court to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucknow">Lucknow</a> in 1775. In 2018 its district was renamed Ayodhya, and the city was joined to the Ayodhya municipal corporation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/faizabad.jpg" alt="Faizabad" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukulfaiz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TilakHall.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
